WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.947
POSITION returns the location of one substring inside another.

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:11.312
It is useful when you need to know whether a delimiter exists or where it occurs.

00:00:11.312 --> 00:00:16.217
For many parsing tasks, SPLIT_PART is clearer when the delimiter already defines meaningful parts.

00:00:16.217 --> 00:00:21.042
POSITION is especially useful during inspection and validation.

00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:26.027
String functions are most useful when the text has a predictable structure.

00:00:26.027 --> 00:00:32.117
Before extracting a substring, confirm the delimiter or pattern really exists.

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:38.432
Regular expressions are powerful, but a complicated regex can become hard to maintain;

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:42.967
use the simplest rule that reliably matches the data you actually have.
